National formats (schema layer only)
------------------------------------
The XSDs below are the issuing authorities' own schemas. They are vendored byte-for-byte except where a
bundle's manifest lists `modifiedFiles`: there the remote `schemaLocation` of an imported schema (the W3C
XML Signature schema, the Polish common types) is rewritten to the vendored copy so nothing is fetched at
runtime. The manifest records the SHA-256 of every downloaded original under `source`. Some of these
files carry no licence text. Only artifacts with qualified publisher grants are distributed.
The remaining inputs are ignored local files; their acquisition recipes and selectors do not imply
permission to redistribute their bytes. Missing selected artifacts produce incomplete validation. Release dates marked "vendoring date" in a manifest mean the
schema states none; they are the day the file was copied (2026-10-16).

