PINT: local qualification only; ZATCA unavailable
------------------------------------------------
Twenty pinned PINT shared/native artifacts are qualified locally for the exact
contracts in the executable selector inventory. Their redistribution grants remain
unresolved, so none ships in default outputs. Missing required native/shared rules
keep public full-source validation incomplete even when UBL syntax passes.
ZATCA SDK artifacts are not integrated. No alternative rules are silently substituted
and no invoice is sent to an external validator. Publisher references and exact
source hashes are retained in the distribution policy and local-source-pins.json.
https://docs.peppol.eu/poac/pint/pint/

